<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ligue 1: Marseille lose to Le Mans after being up 2 goals at home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c08e1aabac7d99c7a86575b1262032a6c513da500ad68755de4f7c681d62e24</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T06:41:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261123-ligue-1-marseille-lose-to-le-mans-after-being-up-2-goals-at-home--101340cda45c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261123-ligue-1-marseille-lose-to-le-mans-after-being-up-2-goals-at-home" /><summary type="html">Olympique de Marseille suffered a home defeat against Le Mans (3–2). Having led 2-0 after 40 minutes thanks to goals from Gouiri (33’) and Paixão (40’), OM collapsed.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Zelensky confirms Ukraine’s military struck Russian ships in Libyan waters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6ba6ba2d38d16f7f08f3bcc1f55a2c79a472e57d7406a89e7a9fd7e64bbf920</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T06:10:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-live-russian-strikes-kill-at-least-15-people-in-kyiv-region-ukraine-says--3314f31f0d59.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-live-russian-strikes-kill-at-least-15-people-in-kyiv-region-ukraine-says" /><summary type="html">Ukraine’s military was responsible for drone attacks on two Russian vessels at the Libyan port of Benghazi Sunday, President Volodymyr Zelensky confirmed Monday. The president alleged that the Russian corvette Merkury had been sunk in the attack. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands rally in Istanbul against Turkey’s crackdown on opposition and media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98d06a03988495ea5a44e05ceb8eb6138a0959b38b597d35b4da48045e581e77</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T02:15:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261123-istanbul-turkey-crackdown-opposition-media-turkey--8822f5f10ff6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261123-istanbul-turkey-crackdown-opposition-media-turkey" /><summary type="html">Thousands marched in Istanbul on Sunday against a widening crackdown on Turkey’s opposition and independent media, days after police raided Sozcu TV and arrested senior staff. The main opposition Yeni Parti organised the protest after authorities installed a government-appointed trustee at the broadcaster, following similar moves against other independent outlets.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Christmas market returns to Paris' Champs Elysées</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1d8bb4a75d45f0a5470468108dbdcceeab1818a49a5b00d25178fdff24b43dd</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T00:46:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-christmas-market-returns-to-paris-champs-elys_es--91de5f49a5cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-christmas-market-returns-to-paris-champs-elys%C3%A9es" /><summary type="html">France 24's Jamie Smith-Maillet reports from the opening of the Paris Christmas market on the Champs Elysées.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's  far-right leader Le Pen denies receiving secrets from civil servant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:171cd599ac481b20bcabc072fc606063e8a62bbc8dfbd7c3bf8aa4352f8b947f</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T00:46:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-france-s-far-right-leader-le-pen-denies-receiving-secrets-from-civil-servant--1820381239f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-france-s-far-right-leader-le-pen-denies-receiving-secrets-from-civil-servant" /><summary type="html">French far-right leader Marine Le Pen Sunday denied receiving confidential information from a civil servant suspected of leaking details of investigations to her National Rally (RN) party, while acknowledging she could not say whether others in the party had benefited.</summary></entry><entry><title>COP31 climate talks in Turkey collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:149b74583cce676403420c2ffcac2244e809f77b29714403acb5ff33864d5e45</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T00:44:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-cop31-climate-talks-collapse--1075c80c2e70.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-cop31-climate-talks-collapse" /><summary type="html">EU member states on Sunday objected to adopting an 11th-hour deal that omitted explicit references to fossil fuels, the bloc's presidency said. The issue remains a major point of contention at the summit, which is taking place amid soaring energy prices and geopolitical tensions fuelled by the war in Iran.</summary></entry><entry><title>Drone strikes hit homes, United Nations building in Sudan's capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1dad2e651d0adf79990978ee445dc00296db4341cbf6f3dae6e9b794e33a6ce</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T00:43:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-drone-strikes-hit-homes-united-nations-building-in-sudan-s-capital--829e941392ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-drone-strikes-hit-homes-united-nations-building-in-sudan-s-capital" /><summary type="html">Drone strikes damaged residential homes and a United Nations building in Sudan's capital Khartoum early Sunday, with the army accusing neighbouring Ethiopia of launching the attacks. The strikes came as drone warfare intensifies in the country's conflict, now in its fourth year.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian ship attacked near Benghazi in suspected drone attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d61e71f15cff6526f73532465cccceef8c3399d537816873043282a829d88410</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T22:37:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261122-russian-ship-attacked-near-benghazi-in-suspected-drone-attack-ukraine--c4ba5ba817ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261122-russian-ship-attacked-near-benghazi-in-suspected-drone-attack-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Authorities in divided Libya's east said a Russian ship docked at the Benghazi port was hit on Sunday in a suspected drone attack, causing a blast but no casualties. There was no immediate claim of responsibility for the strike, but it comes as Ukrainian forces have stepped up their long-range barrages against Russia far beyond the front lines.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel’s Eisenkot slams ‘Jewish terrorism’ after attacks by settlers in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bce7c4d4fa131847e2e526994846fcf5b13ae4257ee309310ecbd2e9203f013d</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T21:29:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261122-israel-s-eisenkot-slams-jewish-terrorism-after-attacks-by-settlers-in-west-bank--d48459cb60f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261122-israel-s-eisenkot-slams-jewish-terrorism-after-attacks-by-settlers-in-west-bank" /><summary type="html">Israeli opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot on Sunday condemned arson attacks by settlers on Palestinian villages in the West Bank as “Jewish terrorism”. Israeli police said they opened an investigation into the attacks, which came nearly a month after an inconclusive election stripped incumbent Prime Minister ⁠Benjamin Netanyahu of his majority.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Democrat Hubbard wins North Carolina recount, clinching historic House majority</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d50ba7c8997954fe7308ad489b281cac49ccfe2d6dfb3d009623d4401a5d5648</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T20:16:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261122-democrat-hubbard-wins-north-carolina-recount-clinching-historic-house-majority--58e941bd0d61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261122-democrat-hubbard-wins-north-carolina-recount-clinching-historic-house-majority" /><summary type="html">Democrat Chuck Hubbard was elected to the US House of Representatives from North Carolina on Sunday after defeating veteran Republican Virginia Foxx, who chairs the powerful House Rules Committee. His victory gave Democrats their best general election result in decades, winning at least 258 seats in the 2026 US midterms.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Russian warship hit by Ukrainian drone at Benghazi naval base, Libyan officials say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:428d1e2fc19f5250ef5ccf49485635d9b6770cd9d4d40281431fd335c4ccf7ff</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T19:41:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261122-russian-warship-hit-by-suspected-ukrainian-drone-at-libya-s-benghazi-naval-base--176c628065fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261122-russian-warship-hit-by-suspected-ukrainian-drone-at-libya-s-benghazi-naval-base" /><summary type="html">A Russian navy corvette docked at the Benghazi naval base ​in eastern Libya was hit on Sunday by a Ukrainian sea drone, according to local officials, hours before a cargo ship was also hit by a sea drone in a second attack. Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky on Monday confirmed that his country's military was behind the strikes.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Burnham, 'Brejoin' &amp; the Ghosts of Brexit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b80191c7782cbba9fec3612545a5c3bb51ec11373024c430892311ee1510587</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T19:37:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261122-burnham-brejoin-the-ghosts-of-brexit--b3f015196424.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261122-burnham-brejoin-the-ghosts-of-brexit" /><summary type="html">“The people of Britain have spoken, and the answer is: we are out.”
 
The words of David Dimbleby at 4.40am on 24 June 2016, as the Brexit referendum result became clear.
 
But nearly a decade on, is Britain changing its mind?
 
Prime Minister Andy Burnham has reopened talks with Brussels, exploring options for a closer relationship with the EU. But the move has drawn criticism from key figures behind Brexit, including Theresa May and Boris Johnson.
 
So what is driving this rethink, and where might it lead?
 
France 24's Gavin Lee speaks to John McTernan, veteran Labour strategist and former adviser to Tony Blair.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Le Pen denies receiving leaked information from French interior ministry official</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c16c11b8430d6bf080cf2736b1ce5dae35e5edca75f91cd7897744af8e5156e6</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T17:47:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261122-le-pen-denies-receiving-leaked-information-from-french-interior-ministry-official--9d27750a0e78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261122-le-pen-denies-receiving-leaked-information-from-french-interior-ministry-official" /><summary type="html">French far-right leader Marine Le Pen on Sunday said she did not receive, nor ask for, confidential information on an investigation into her party from a senior interior ministry official. She however could not say if other party members had benefited from the leaks. Hugues Moutouh, the civil servant under suspicion, has denied the allegations and asked to be relieved of his duties pending a probe.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Ligue 1: PSG extend winning run at Nice (3-2) but lose Désiré Doué to injury</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00b5871268f39524ae143bf53fcdd85f9d4f71038a9def670f44fb35c360bb1d</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T16:55:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261122-ligue-1-psg-extend-winning-run-at-nice-3-2-but-lose-d_sir_-dou_-to-injury--300e3e4fab37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261122-ligue-1-psg-extend-winning-run-at-nice-3-2-but-lose-d%C3%A9sir%C3%A9-dou%C3%A9-to-injury" /><summary type="html">A bittersweet victory for PSG at Nice on Saturday evening. The Parisians strengthened their grip on top spot in Ligue 1, but lost Désiré Doué for several months after the forward suffered a serious knee injury.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Drone strikes hit homes and UN building in Sudan's Khartoum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df48a4346a95be47dd9a4d3802c85d4bbd1f4cf4b9be24ead8762fce837965f3</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T16:38:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261122-drone-strikes-hit-homes-and-un-building-in-sudan-s-khartoum--8d694ed4036b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261122-drone-strikes-hit-homes-and-un-building-in-sudan-s-khartoum" /><summary type="html">Drone strikes damaged residential homes and a United Nations building in Sudan's capital Khartoum early Sunday, with the army accusing neighbouring Ethiopia of launching the attacks. The strikes came as drone warfare intensifies in the country's conflict, now in its fourth year.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank attacks: Opposition leader Eisenkot decries "Jewish terrorism"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e484ebc2a34e592f8cc5d3b60525c1afa2c7a6b6acdb91966012bb40da13dc3</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T16:25:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/west-bank-attacks-opposition-leader-eisenkot-decries-jewish-terrorism--0689dfc975ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-attacks-opposition-leader-eisenkot-decries-jewish-terrorism" /><summary type="html">Israeli authorities have opened an investigation after Palestinian vehicles and properties were set on fire in three villages in the occupied West Bank. Israeli soldiers were deployed to the area following the attacks, which local residents said were carried out by Israeli settlers. Gadi Eisenkot, a rival of outgoing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, condemned the acts on X, describing them as “Jewish terrorism”. Antonia Kerrigan reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian strike kills 2 in Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfabd231fcaadb471519142aa99803e74c9a7c6a281f2b0bb100658ce4041e3a</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T16:23:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russian-strike-kills-2-in-kyiv--c902d721aaa7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-strike-kills-2-in-kyiv" /><summary type="html">A Russian attack struck an apartment building in the village of Dymer, just north of Kyiv, on Sunday, killing at least two people and wounding four others. The morning strike destroyed a five-storey building, while rescuers evacuated nine people, including a child. At least 11 others are believed to remain trapped under the rubble.</summary></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Xi hosts Trump and Putin, COP31 and new French protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d09982b52e27ab53b0951996333e81e0bf586b8e0a7fee3f6f2ebcd11eddfa9a</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T14:22:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261122-the-week-in-pictures-xi-hosts-trump-and-putin-cop31-and-more-french-protests--4e7f9837e4c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261122-the-week-in-pictures-xi-hosts-trump-and-putin-cop31-and-more-french-protests" /><summary type="html">From the unprecedented Shenzhen summit in China that saw President Xi Jinping host his US and Russian counterparts, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin, to tough talks at COP31 in Antalya, Turkey and another week of French protests over the cost of living, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the most striking images from the past week.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>"It can take years": Why the AI Riemann proof is far from settled</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cac7e58da2387f63de5af7e8e904cb5c9874167308a25e77950e06aa4f0e551b</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T14:18:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261122-it-can-take-years-why-the-ai-riemann-proof-is-far-from-settled--1f21c7349a19.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261122-it-can-take-years-why-the-ai-riemann-proof-is-far-from-settled" /><summary type="html">AI claimed another major scalp in maths on Friday, as Anthropic mathematician Levent Alpöge published what he says is a proof of the Riemann hypothesis, a Millennium Prize Problem, in 17 million lines of code that no human has read in full. Physicist Tony Padilla tells Tech 24 that verification could take years, and that Alpöge should share how he got there.</summary><category term="Tech 24" /></entry><entry><title>Israel investigates West Bank fires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0f24a574b534f5f591b7a999b21d26f1e47ab9a9817c76a5b4415559942399c</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T13:47:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-investigates-west-bank-fires--de82d2e7e2ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-investigates-west-bank-fires" /><summary type="html">Israeli authorities have opened an investigation after Palestinian vehicles and properties were vandalised and set on fire in four villages in the occupied West Bank, in attacks local activists say were carried out by Israeli settlers. Around eight vehicles were reportedly torched and racist slogans sprayed on walls, prompting Israeli soldiers and police to deploy to the area. The attacks come amid a surge in settler violence since the outbreak of the Gaza war in October 2023, with more than 1,100 Palestinians killed by Israeli soldiers or settlers in the West Bank since then, according to an AFP tally. They also follow recent sanctions announced by the UK and Australia against eight Israeli companies involved in settlement activity. France 24 correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky shares further details from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 COP31 ends without deal as EU rejects text for omitting mention of fossil fuels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3155570198a214553006d311f8d146366043dfa276844445c4ff3ac40318858a</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T12:22:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/environment/20261121-latest-cop31-deal-sidesteps-fossil-fuels-amid-growing-divisions--4a362b91171e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261121-latest-cop31-deal-sidesteps-fossil-fuels-amid-growing-divisions" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia factory hit by deadly blaze: Three killed and 36 missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc6fa2b6d65427ad83bd0329870b8be41f7af51399bcd00e75efbea874368a73</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T12:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/indonesia-factory-hit-by-deadly-blaze-three-killed-and-36-missing--ac78e10c1ede.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/indonesia-factory-hit-by-deadly-blaze-three-killed-and-36-missing" /><summary type="html">At least three people have been killed and dozens are missing after a fire broke out at a factory in Indonesia producing sweets and snack products. Fifteen people were rescued alive from the plant, while firefighters were still battling flames in several parts of the facility more than 12 hours after the blaze began. The cause of the fire remains unknown, but survivors said it started in a cooling unit on the third floor.</summary></entry><entry><title>Former Italian police chief found dead</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:325bc9adc27d18b58d69836b9ce23a85270e90a366493e590bba99cd04f68c08</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T10:25:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/former-italian-police-chief-found-dead--b581330f274d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/former-italian-police-chief-found-dead" /><summary type="html">Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni has expressed shock following the death of a former national police chief, whose body was found on Saturday. He had been under investigation over an alleged cover-up in an inquiry into a bombing linked to organised crime in Sicily. Jennie Shin reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Princess of Wales opens up about cancer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e59ce4d2e66d8a0318b19960895eee9b44fa9136b3bf226652ed8afcb9334c0</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T10:07:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/princess-of-wales-opens-up-about-cancer--bfdd7bab3bf7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/princess-of-wales-opens-up-about-cancer" /><summary type="html">A new documentary titled Heal follows Britain’s Princess Catherine as she navigates life since her cancer diagnosis in 2024. The film tracks the 44-year-old as she attempts to climb the highest mountains in Scotland, England and Wales within 24 hours. In the trailer, she reflects on healing as a journey. Ophelie Jacobson reports.</summary></entry></feed>
